#: build/admin/settings.e9073e3b.js:16
msgid "How to connect Airbnb and Booking.com"
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/settings.e9073e3b.js:16
msgid "Import (OTA → website): in Airbnb (Availability › Connect calendars › Export calendar) or the Booking.com extranet (Rates & Availability › Sync calendars › Export), copy the unit’s link and add it here with “Add link”."
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/settings.e9073e3b.js:16
msgid "Export (website → OTA): copy this unit’s “Export to Airbnb” / “Export to Booking.com” link and paste it into the same screen of that channel under “Import calendar”. Each channel gets its own link so its own bookings are never sent back to it."
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/settings.e9073e3b.js:16
msgid "Repeat for every unit. The links are secret: if one leaks, use “New export links” and paste the new link into the channels again."
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/settings.e9073e3b.js:16
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/settings.e9073e3b.js:16
msgid "iCal only shares busy/free dates — no prices, minimum stay, guest names or messages."
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/settings.e9073e3b.js:16
msgid "There is always a delay: the website reads the channels every 15 minutes (and right before each website booking), but Airbnb and Booking.com decide themselves how often they read our link — sometimes only every few hours. In peak season consider manual confirmation of OTA bookings."
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/settings.e9073e3b.js:16
msgid "If an imported booking overlaps a website booking, it is shown in red on the calendar and on the dashboard, and an e-mail is sent. Nothing is cancelled automatically — resolve it with the guest and the channel."
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/settings.e9073e3b.js:16
msgid "Full guide (Croatian and English): docs/ical-setup.md in the plugin folder."
msgstr ""

